            "review_title": "Review at Nuong Cay - Hotpot & Grill",
            "review_text": "Carlton\nDa Nang, Vietnam27 contributions\n0\nDecent quality, amazing value\nJan 2019 • Couples\nWe popped in here a couple of nights ago on the basis of the reviews, as luckily we are staying nearby. On balance, we were not disappointed.\n\nWe arrived around 20:00 to find it almost empty apart from one other table. It is a very big place so that felt perhaps a little awkward. It was helped by the fact that the PA was blasting what I assume to be Vietnamese pop songs and ballads at an almost deafening (and certainly uncomfortable) volume.\n\nFortunately, that's where the complaints end. The place gradually started getting busier during our meal, with a number of large parties coming in. We seemed to be the only foreigners, which we personally took to be a good sign. \n\nThe menu had a very good selection of dishes including a lot of vegetable ones. The service was friendly and attentive, without being suffocating. And the quality of the food when it arrived was good. Special mention for the catfish Hotpot and the stir fried okra. \n\nFinally,the value for money was exceptional. Meal for two with a number of different dishes and a drink each, and we had plenty of change from 200,000 VND. And our friendly waiter even politely declined the modest tip we offered at the end.\n\nAll in all, definitely worth a visit, especially if you're nearby. We'll probably eat here again before we leave.\nRead more\nWritten January 11, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
